 "fieldData": {
  "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Affiliate Page Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is an affiliate landing page?\", \"a\": \"An affiliate landing page is a page an affiliate publishes between a traffic source, such as a search result or a video, and the merchant's sales page. Its one job is a click on the tracking link. ClickBank calls this a bridge page, because the reader crosses it on the way to the offer.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do you create an affiliate landing page?\", \"a\": \"Start with one offer and the evidence only you have, such as test notes. Then describe the page to Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder'>AI landing page builder</a> with your links and disclosure sentence. It builds the page, tags each button, and saves every click to a table.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is the best free landing page builder for affiliate marketing?\", \"a\": \"Pick one that lets you put your own tracking ID on every link and records outbound clicks without a visitor limit. Check whether a custom domain uses credits or costs extra. Ask whether you can export the code too. Emergent is free to start, and the free tier covers building and publishing a page with a live URL.\"}, {\"q\": \"What do good affiliate landing page examples have in common?\", \"a\": \"Proof that the writer used the product: original photos, measurements, and a list of what it was tested against. They use few buttons and put each one where a decision gets made. Galleries of affiliate marketing landing page examples mostly show layout; borrow the structure from them, never the copy.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should an affiliate marketing landing page include?\", \"a\": \"A headline that names the product and who it suits, then evidence such as test notes or a comparison table. Add a plain disclosure, and give each button a sub ID of its own. Pages about a costly product also earn a short section on who should skip it.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is an affiliate program landing page used for?\", \"a\": \"A merchant uses it to recruit affiliates. The page states the commission, the credit window, and the traffic it accepts, then takes applications. On a page built with Emergent, each application lands in a database you own. A thank you page can then tell applicants when to expect an answer.\"}, {\"q\": \"Where do you add the disclosure on affiliate landing pages?\", \"a\": \"Near the top, before the first link a reader can click, and again beside any link far down the page. For web pages, the FTC's Endorsement Guides say a disclosure should be unavoidable. A disclosure tucked behind a link fails that test; keep the sentence itself on the page.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do you track clicks on affiliate marketing landing pages?\", \"a\": \"Give each link a sub ID that names the page and the button, such as stove-specs. If your network accepts sub IDs, as impact.com does, its reports show which value drove the most conversions. Log every outbound click on your own side too, and you can see which buttons draw clicks that never turn into sales.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can you make affiliate landing pages without a website?\", \"a\": \"Yes. A single page at its own address can carry the review and its tracked buttons with no blog behind it. Emergent can host it on a custom domain, which uses credits, and on paid plans the code exports to your GitHub repository. Add a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder/404-page'>404 page</a> that sends readers of broken links back to the review.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do you set up links on a landing page for affiliate marketing?\", \"a\": \"Add rel=sponsored to the anchor tag of every merchant link, buttons included. Google asks sites in affiliate programs to mark these links, whether they were placed by hand or generated by a script. Links to your own pages stay as they are.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
 }
}